// Fixed-width SIMD vectors: u8x16, s8x16, u16x8, s16x8, u32x4, s32x4,
// u64x2, s64x2, f32x4 and f64x2, and their 256-bit forms such as s16x16.
// Import the module and call its operations through the alias:
//
//     Simd :: #import "simd"
//     sum := Simd.Add(Simd.Load(s16x8, row, 0), Simd.Splat(s16x8, 1))
//
// Every operation gives the same bits on every target: C uses SSE2..AVX2,
// NEON or WebAssembly SIMD128 where they match, and Go, the VM and other
// C compilers compute lane by lane. Integer lanes wrap unless the operation
// saturates. Operations that move data between lanes, such as Shuffle,
// ByteShuffle, AlignBytes, Narrow and InterleaveLow, work on each 128-bit
// block of a 256-bit vector on its own.
//
// Lane-wise arithmetic: Add, Sub, Mul, Div (float), AddSat, SubSat (8 and
// 16-bit lanes), Min, Max, Average (u8, u16, rounding up), MulHigh (16-bit),
// MulHighRound (s16, Q15 rounding), Abs, Neg, Sign(a, b) (signed lanes: a
// negated where b < 0 and 0 where b is 0), AbsDiff(a, b) (|a - b| in the
// unsigned lanes of the same width).
// Bits: And, Or, Xor, AndNot(a, b) = a & ~b, Not.
// Compare: Equal, Less, Greater give all-ones lanes where true; float
// lanes give the unsigned vector of the same width. Select(mask, a, b)
// takes bits from a where the mask is set and from b elsewhere.
// Shifts: ShiftLeft, ShiftRight (arithmetic for signed lanes, logical for
// unsigned lanes) and ShiftRightRound take one count; ShiftLeftLanes and
// ShiftRightLanes take a vector of counts. A count of the lane width or
// more gives 0, or the sign for an arithmetic shift. ShiftRightRound(v, n)
// is (v >> n) plus the last bit shifted out.
// Bytes: ShiftBytesLeft, ShiftBytesRight and AlignBytes(high, low, n) take
// a constant byte count; ByteShuffle(table, indices) gives 0 for an index
// of 16 or more.
// Lanes: Make(T, ...), Splat(T, x), Zero(T), Lane(v, i), WithLane(v, i, x),
// Shuffle(v, i0, i1, ...) with constant indices.
// Memory: Load(T, data, at), LoadLow(T, data, at) reads the low 64 bits
// and zeroes the rest; Store(data, at, v), StoreLow(data, at, v). Slices
// and arrays are checked once per access; pointers are not checked.
// Gather(table, indices) reads 32-bit lanes from a table.
// Width: WidenLow, WidenHigh (half the lanes, twice as wide), Widen (a
// 128-bit vector to 256 bits), Narrow(T, a, b) with saturation,
// MulWideLow, MulWideHigh, MulAddPairs (s16 pairs to s32), MulAddPairsSat
// (u8 by s8 pairs to s16, saturating), AddPairs, SumAbsDiff (u8 to u64).
// Reductions: ReduceAdd, ReduceMin, ReduceMax, ReduceMaxIndex (the first
// lane holding the maximum), AllZero.
// Types: Reinterpret(T, v) keeps the bits, Convert(T, v) converts between
// integer and float lanes of the same width (float to integer truncates
// and saturates; NaN gives 0), Low, High and Combine split and join
// 256-bit vectors, InterleaveLow and InterleaveHigh merge lanes.
